      "observed": "The USB-A host connector J38 has its D- line (pin 2) routed through U56 I/O1 to U50 HSD1+ and then to Module2 USB2_P, while its D+ line (pin 3) is routed through U56 I/O2 to U50 HSD1- and then to Module2 USB2_N.",
      "expected": "For a USB host port, J38 D+ should be routed to the positive differential input (U50 HSD1+) and ultimately Module2 USB2_P, and J38 D- should be routed to U50 HSD1- and Module2 USB2_N. The USB-C path through U23/U18/U50 is wired this way, so the USB-A host path is inconsistent.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"65\") (name \"NET0030\") ... (node (ref \"J38\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"D-\") ... (node (ref \"U56\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"I/O1\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"121\") (name \"NET0166\") ... (node (ref \"U50\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"HSD1+\") ... (node (ref \"U56\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"I/O1\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"141\") (name \"NET0205\") ... (node (ref \"Module2\") (pin \"105\") (pinfunction \"USB2_P\") ... (node (ref \"U50\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"D+\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"88\") (name \"NET0081\") ... (node (ref \"J38\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"D+\") ... (node (ref \"U56\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"I/O2\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"125\") (name \"NET0178\") ... (node (ref \"U50\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"HSD1-\") ... (node (ref \"U56\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"I/O2\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"130\") (name \"NET0183\") ... (node (ref \"Module2\") (pin \"103\") (pinfunction \"USB2_N\") ... (node (ref \"U50\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"D-\") ...)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "When the analog switch selects the USB-A host port, the CM4 receives USB D+ and D- reversed. USB devices plugged into J38 would likely fail to enumerate or behave erratically.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a clear USB host data-line polarity error: the USB-A connector J38 D+/D- are swapped through U56 and U50 into the CM4 USB differential pair, which would make the USB host port behave differently from the intended design."
}

